            <ArticleTitle>A case of Carney complex presenting as acute testicular pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>360-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0974-7796.184887</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case of a 7-year-old boy who presented with testicular pain but was found to have bilateral testicular lesions later confirmed as Sertoli cell tumors. Genetic testing confirmed a PRKAR1A gene mutation consistent with Carney complex, a rare genetic disorder characterized by skin lesions, myxomas, and multiple endocrine neoplasms. A review of the condition is made highlighting the association with testicular tumors, particularly of Sertoli cell origin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
